# Added 18-Aug-2026 - deploy/deploy.sh (and any future .sh) must reach
# the Linux VPS with LF line endings, not CRLF, or bash fails with
# "bad interpreter" on the shebang line. The committed blob is already
# LF (checked via `git show :deploy/deploy.sh | xxd` - confirmed, not
# assumed), but that currently depends on every future contributor's
# own core.autocrlf setting rather than being guaranteed by the repo
# itself - this makes it explicit and machine-independent.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Added 18-Aug-2026, same reasoning - systemd unit files are also
# consumed on the Linux VPS (deploy/turion-event-driven.service,
# turion-engine-alert.service). systemd's own INI-style parser is
# generally more tolerant of a stray \r than bash's shebang line, but
# there's no reason to rely on that tolerance when the same one-line
# fix already used for *.sh covers this too.
*.service text eol=lf
